First of all, Mr. Speaker, I should like to point out an inaccuracy. I think the hon. member for Sainte-Marie made a 21611-47}
Company of Young Canadians Act lapsus by referring to students, since it is not stipulated anywhere, and it is not the government's intention, that the Council of the Company will be restricted to the student class which is a minority, and a privileged one at that, among our youth.
As to the process of appointing these representatives, I would say to the hon. member for Sainte-Marie that the government will follow the same pattern that it applies for instance in the case of the directors of the C.B.C., or the members of the Board of the Canadian Radio-Television Commission, whose integrity or objectivity has never to my knowledge been questioned by anybody-not even by the hon. member for Sainte-Marie.
